        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "program",
        "groupId": "bedb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 2,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<p>The&nbsp;Social&nbsp;Welfare&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;major&nbsp;is&nbsp;a&nbsp;designated&nbsp;“group&nbsp;major”&nbsp;grounded&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;liberal&nbsp;arts,&nbsp;rather&nbsp;than&nbsp;specialized&nbsp;training&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;profession&nbsp;of&nbsp;social&nbsp;work.&nbsp;</p><p>The&nbsp;curriculum,&nbsp;as&nbsp;reflected&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;core&nbsp;major&nbsp;courses,&nbsp;focuses&nbsp;both&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;history&nbsp;and&nbsp;institutions&nbsp;of&nbsp;social&nbsp;work&nbsp;as&nbsp;a&nbsp;field&nbsp;of&nbsp;activity&nbsp;and&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;welfare&nbsp;state&nbsp;as&nbsp;a&nbsp;collective&nbsp;enterprise&nbsp;addressing&nbsp;human&nbsp;need.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p>Students&nbsp;gain&nbsp;knowledge&nbsp;of&nbsp;organized&nbsp;networks&nbsp;of&nbsp;public&nbsp;and&nbsp;private&nbsp;social&nbsp;services,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;basic&nbsp;practice&nbsp;methods&nbsp;associated&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;social&nbsp;work&nbsp;profession.&nbsp;In&nbsp;doing&nbsp;so,&nbsp;students&nbsp;acquire&nbsp;the&nbsp;knowledge&nbsp;needed&nbsp;to&nbsp;understand,&nbsp;address,&nbsp;and&nbsp;actively&nbsp;participate&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;amelioration&nbsp;of&nbsp;critical&nbsp;social&nbsp;problems&nbsp;in&nbsp;American&nbsp;Society.</p><p></p><p><strong>For&nbsp;more&nbsp;information:</strong></p><p>Jeremy&nbsp;Urban,&nbsp;Undergraduate&nbsp;Major&nbsp;Advisor</p><p>UC&nbsp;Berkeley&nbsp;School&nbsp;of&nbsp;Social&nbsp;Welfare</p><p>email:&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:swugadvisor@berkeley.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">swugadvisor@berkeley.edu</a></p><p><a href=\"https://socialwelfare.berkeley.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://socialwelfare.berkeley.edu/</a></p>",
        "groupId": "c0db6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 3,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "important major information",
        "groupId": "b8db6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 4,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<p><strong>Social Welfare is a high-demand major.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>The five prerequisites must be completed with a minimum letter grade of C prior to enrollment of the first semester at Berkeley.</p><p>This applies to courses taken at Berkeley or equivalent courses taken at other institutions.</p><p><br></p><p>Note: Prerequisites completed prior to Spring 2006 will count with a C- or P grade.</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Required Lower-division requirements:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Psychology 1, or 2</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stats 2, 20, or 21, Soc 5, Poli Sci 3 <strong>or any course that satisfies the College of Letters and Science Quantitative Reasoning Requirement</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sociology 1, 3, 3A, or 3AC</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>The College of Letters and Science Reading and Composition requirement</strong>. (This is a 2-course series. At UCB: Reading and Composition A + Reading and Composition B)</li><li>Highly recommended lower-division requirements:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">It is suggested that three other courses (introductory anthropology, introductory economics, and introductory political science, as listed below) should be taken as preparation for the major, but these courses are not required to declare the major.</li></ul>",
        "groupId": "badb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 5,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "exam credit",
        "groupId": "bcdb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 6,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<ul><li>AP&nbsp;Psychology&nbsp;:&nbsp;score&nbsp;of&nbsp;3&nbsp;or&nbsp;higher</li></ul>",
        "groupId": "bddb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 7,
        "area": "General"
      }
    ],
